#4803
Qitiexi Street~
   You weave in and out of the large group of people assembled before you.
Judging by the worn depressions in the gravel street, you would guess that
this was one of the busiest places in the city. Vendors call out from the
sides of the street, babies cry, angry shouts from disgruntled traders - it's
alive with sound.
   Just to the southwest, the top of a huge temple climbs into the sky,
dwarfing the surrounding buildings. To the east, the city bank serves all who
visit the city while to the west, a shabbily-constructed building is filled
with people.
