paper note rules gamble~
0~
+-+-Gambling 101-+-+
You can play three different gambling games here. Two of them involve dice,
and the last involves the Wheel of Misfortune.
 
Sevens:
This simple dice game involves the rolling of two dice. You can bet on the
total being less than 7 (low roll), equal to 7 (seven) or greater than 7
(high roll). Ping Xiao's gambling house pays 1:1 odds on both the low and
high rolls, and 4:1 on the seven.
Command usage: sevens bet low|seven|high
 
SicBo:
This dice game is slightly more complex than Sevens, but offers a much greater
variety of betting. Use the command 'sicbo help' for detailed rules on playing,
and read odds for a layout of Ping Xiao's gambling house odds.
Command usage:  sicbo bet type value value
 
Wheel of Misfortune:
This strange, magical wheel is capable of applying various magical effects upon
the spinner. Also, standard payouts are given for certain slots on the wheel.
Costs 1000 per play. Play at your own risk.
Command usage:  spin
~
E
odds odd~
0~
+-+- Odds -+-+
If you win, you get payed off according to the odds of the bet you made.
For example, if you bet 400 gold and win on a 4:1 bet, you'll win 1600
gold.
 
Sevens.
High/Low : 1:1
Seven    : 4:1
 
Sicbo.
Diceface : 1:1 for each dice that comes up your number
Twoface  : 5:1
Totals   : 60:1 if you bet on 4 or 17
           18:1 if you bet on 5 or 16
           14:1 if you bet on 6 or 15
           12:1 if you bet on 7 or 14
            8:1 if you bet on 8 or 13
            6:1 if you bet on 9 or 12
            6:1 if you bet on 10 or 11
Range    : 1:1
Triple   : 150:1, for any triple 24:1
Anypair  : 8:1
~
S
